# Shell scripts run on the Linux mini PC — must keep LF endings.
# Without this, Git on Windows checks them out with CRLF and `sh script.sh`
# fails with a "\r: command not found" / bad interpreter error.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for container/infra files consumed inside Linux images.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md must stay byte-identical, and scripts/check_docs_sync.sh
# enforces that with a byte comparison. Windows would check them out as CRLF while
# a Linux session writes LF, which breaks the comparison for a reason that has
# nothing to do with their content. Pin every Markdown file to LF so the check
# means what it says on both platforms.
*.md text eol=lf
